<title>USA: Century Q1 shr $0.84 loss, with write-down.</title>
<headline>Century Q1 shr $0.84 loss, with write-down.</headline>
<dateline>NEW CANAAN, Conn. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>FYE 1997	    FYE 1996</p>
<p>				     3 Months Ended  3 Months Ended</p>
<p>					 8/31/96	     8/31/95</p>
<p>Revenues			  $153,004,000	$116,627,000</p>
<p>Operating Income Before</p>
<p>Depreciation and Amortization</p>
<p> and Australian Operations    77,342,000	  61,514,000</p>
<p>Operating Loss of Australian</p>
<p> Operations			(45,520,000)		   --</p>
<p>Operating (Loss) Income	(24,314,000)	 13,789,000</p>
<p>Tax Benefit			  6,598,000	   4,806,000</p>
<p>Net Loss			   (61,212,000)	(21,917,000)</p>
<p>Net Loss Per Share		     ($.84)		($.31)</p>
<p>Average Number of Shares</p>
<p> Outstanding			74,069,000	  73,583,000</p>
<p>NOTE: First quarter earnings results include a $40 million write-down of the company's investment in the Australian Pay Television business.</p>
<p>Revenue from the company's consolidated wireless telephone operations were $32,365,000 for the three months ended August 31, an 20.2 percent increase over the year-ago figure.  </p>
<p>Operating income before depreciation and amortization for the wireless telephone business was $15,082,000, a 12.8 percent increase over the year-ago figure.</p>
<p>Full company name is Century Communications Corp.</p>
</text>
